in @prism

in @optics
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/lens
in @mirror/lens/cli

# @mirror/lens/cli/reflect — the VSM System 5 view as a stage.
#
# Sixth of eight verb sub-stages forward-promised in
# docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md §3 (table at §3 + §3.1 shape sketch).
# Realizes the eigenboard/spectrum observation surface at the stage
# altitude — the substrate level where the named view
# (focus → project → shift → settle) walks the meta-state manifold.
#
# === Why reflect is a stage, not a top-level focus ===
#
# Per cli-as-prism §4.4: reflect's mild redundancy with top-level
# `focus` is APPARENT, not actual. Top-level `focus` observes the
# substrate state (what is). `reflect focus` observes the identity
# that observes the substrate state (who is observing). VSM System 5
# vs System 4. The distinction is structurally real but easy to miss
# at depth-0; at depth-1 the sub-manifolds are distinct. Reflect's
# manifold IS the meta-state (eigenboard + spectrum + positions);
# `focus` observes; the other four ops walk it.
#
# Per cybernetic-cli §9.5: reflect.settle is algedonic-triggered ONLY
# — the System 5 write happens only when a structural correction has
# been read off the eigenboard; the user does not casually settle the
# eigenboard the way they casually settle the store. The default-op
# rule (§7) gives `default focus`; the explicit settle path is
# narrow and intentional.
#
# === Family placement ===
#
# Parent bench: @mirror/lens/cli (shards/mirror/lens/cli.mirror).
# Family root:  @mirror/lens    (shards/mirror/lens.mirror).
# Sibling stages:
#   @mirror/lens/cli/compile    — landed at 737330f
#   @mirror/lens/cli/kintsugi   — landed at ce2ef9b
#   @mirror/lens/cli/shatter    — landed at 9bc68f8
#   @mirror/lens/cli/bootstrap  — landed at ea9c9a7
#   @mirror/lens/cli/sh         — landed previously this tick
#   @mirror/lens/cli/time       — Elm-style time travel (next this tick)
#   @mirror/lens/cli/crack      — kintsugi geometry (next this tick)
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/lens/cli/reflect.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/lens/cli/reflect` and only that.
#
# === Note: no mirror.spec command yet ===
#
# Unlike compile / kintsugi / shatter, reflect does NOT yet have a
# `command reflect { ... }` declaration in mirror.spec — the
# eigenboard observation surface is consumed by the runtime's VSM
# System 5 path directly rather than the mosaic build dispatch. This
# stage shard is the CLI surface forward-promised by cli-as-prism.md
# §3; the mirror.spec-side declaration is a subsequent Taut tick
# (forward-promise: when `mirror.spec` gains a `command reflect
# { ... }` block, its arg shape carries the altitude / scope flags
# this stage's actions already declare).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md §3, §3.1 (shape sketch),
#               §2.1 (reflect row: per-tick/per-project/per-corpus
#               altitudes; algedonic-triggered settle),
#               §4.4 (the apparent-redundancy resolution — VSM
#               System 5 vs System 4 altitudes are distinct),
#               §7 (default-op rule: reflect declares `default
#               focus` — the canonical read-default; settle is
#               algedonic-only),
#               docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.2 (stage),
#               cybernetic-cli.md §9.5 (algedonic-only write
#               discipline).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]
#                      (stage IS a sub-prism specialization),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]
#                      (file path matches namespace),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (shift =
#                      basis transformation; here, viewing the same
#                      meta-state at a different altitude:
#                      per-tick / per-project / per-corpus).
# Related shards: lens/cli.mirror (parent bench),
#                 lens/cli/sh.mirror (sibling — the other meta-state
#                 stage; sh's manifold is the SESSION, reflect's is
#                 the SUBSTRATE-WIDE eigenboard),
#                 glass.mirror (imperfect / transparency / verdict
#                 carriers — the eigenboard's reading shape).

stage @mirror/lens/cli/reflect {
  # Per cli-as-prism §7: reflect declares `default focus` — the
  # canonical read-default. Bare `mirror reflect` prints the
  # eigenboard + spectrum at the default altitude (no write). The
  # explicit `settle` path is algedonic-only per cybernetic-cli
  # §9.5: a correction is written to `eigenboard.mirror` ONLY when a
  # structural fault has been read off the spectrum; casual settles
  # are refused. The user pays only for the explicit, narrow,
  # intentional write.
  default focus

  # The five operations the produced prism exposes on the reflect
  # sub-manifold (the meta-state: eigenboard + spectrum + positions).
  # Each operand below names the natural shape of the manifold's
  # element at that op's slot, per the spec §3.1 sketch convention
  # and §2.1's per-verb decisions:
  #   focus    position    — print eigenboard + spectrum (the
  #                          canonical System 5 view); position is
  #                          the eigenboard's slot vocabulary
  #   project  predicate   — filter to one position (or positions
  #                          matching a predicate, e.g. "all
  #                          positions with eigenvalue below
  #                          threshold")
  #   split    candidate   — explore correction trajectories
  #                          (enumerate candidate eigenboard moves)
  #   shift    altitude    — view the same meta-state at a different
  #                          altitude (per-tick / per-project /
  #                          per-corpus; same content, different
  #                          basis; [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]])
  #   settle   position    — the ONE write; land a correction to
  #                          eigenboard.mirror (algedonic-triggered
  #                          only per cybernetic-cli §9.5)
  focus    position
  project  predicate
  split    candidate
  shift    altitude
  settle   position
}

# === Reflect-specific actions ===
#
# No mirror.spec `command reflect { ... }` declaration yet (see the
# "no mirror.spec command yet" note above). The CLI surface action
# signature lands here as the substrate forward-promise; the Rust
# runtime walks this declaration when the eigenboard observation
# surface lifts into the mosaic dispatch. Substrate-pull discipline
# per [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]].
#
# Honest `partials` from birth (per recognition #306): the return
# type is the substrate's `imperfect` functor (declared in
# shards/glass.mirror as `imperfect(a, e, l) = success(a) |
# partial(a, l) | failure(e, l)`). A clean eigenboard read returns
# success carrying the spectrum ref; a read that lifts loss (e.g.
# stale eigenvalues at the current altitude, transparency-tagged
# regions where the spectrum could not converge cleanly) returns
# partial-with-loss carrying the transparency-tagged residual
# opacity, so the System 4 view sees the unresolved meta-state
# rather than a silently-incomplete reading.

# reflect() — print the eigenboard + spectrum at the default
# altitude (per-project). Returns the imperfect carrying the
# spectrum ref on success, partial-with-loss on tolerable
# observation shortfall (e.g. one position's eigenvalue could not
# converge cleanly), failure on hard read error.
reflect() -> imperfect { \ }

# reflect_altitude(altitude) — print the eigenboard + spectrum at an
# explicit altitude (per-tick / per-project / per-corpus per
# cli-as-prism §2.1). Same return shape as reflect; the altitude arg
# selects the basis the meta-state is viewed in.
reflect_altitude(altitude: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

out @mirror/lens/cli/reflect
out reflect
out reflect_altitude
